# Cloudflare edge caching rules. The adapter appends its own /_astro/* Cache-Control line to this
# file during the build; everything here is ours.
#
# Why HTML is not edge-cached: HTML is served through the Worker, and those responses carry no ETag
# and no Last-Modified (static assets like /_astro/* and /makraz.vcf do). `must-revalidate` with no
# validator gives the edge nothing to revalidate against, so it keeps serving whatever it cached.
# That bit three deploys in a row on 2026-08-04 — stale pages twice, and once a cached 404 for
# /en/blog/vitrine-ou-plateforme, which is the kind of thing that gets a URL dropped from an index.
#
# CDN-Cache-Control targets the edge only, so browsers still honour the Cache-Control below and
# fingerprinted assets stay cached at the edge for a year.
/*
  CDN-Cache-Control: no-store

# Fingerprinted filenames, so these are safe to cache hard in both places.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  CDN-Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
